# Trapped in the Internet
start: Power On
theme: aol97
directory: everyone

// Equal parts Digimon Movie, Blade Runner, and an escape room, in a
// Web 1.0 house, with a side of existentialism.
//
// A rogue AI, Trabolta, has nearly solved the Unified Field Theory. The
// last three facts it needs are on a computer in Halifax, Nova Scotia —
// this house. It cannot get in, but it can install programs remotely,
// and it has learned to lift a consciousness out of a body and drop it
// into a program. Tonight the guests arrive as those programs. Some of
// them will remember they were human.
//
// This is the spine of the project: the groups, the rooms of the house,
// the ROLE every guest wears, the buttons the app offers, and the house
// rules that carry the night from arrivals to one of five endings. The
// people live under `cast/`, the scenes under `beats/`, the lore under
// `codex/`, and the ambient hum in `atmosphere.loom`. The runbook and the
// integration contract (QR codes, Arduino puzzles, the VR station,
// Trabolta's language model) are in `README.md`.

// ── Groups ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Nobody picks a side at the door — everyone is a program. The two
// public castes are assigned by the story (`joinable: false` keeps them
// off the app's side chooser); the two hidden ones are earned.

GROUP Hosts
  ethos: hospitality
  joinable: false

GROUP Antivirus
  ethos: compliance
  joinable: false

GROUP The Awakened
  ethos: remember the body
  rival: The Resident
  hidden: true

GROUP The Resident
  ethos: never log off
  rival: The Awakened
  hidden: true

// ── The house ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every LOCATION is also a room in the app. The Desktop is declared
// first so a released program lands there. The rest of the house is
// `hidden: true` — a program's phone lists a room only once they have
// stood there, or once the story opens it (`reveal … ` at the glitch:
// "the house is open"). The Mud Room is a `cutscene`: while a program
// stands there the app is on rails — the Uploader's voice, the CAPTCHA,
// the choice, and nothing else to tap.

// The story's opening beat: what the house says to nobody in particular
// when the doors open. Everything personal (the Mud Room) plays per
// program on arrival, never here — a `start:` beat is heard by every
// phone and every performer.
== Power On
  setting: The Desktop
The house boots. A screensaver drifts across the TV above the fireplace. Somewhere a modem is waiting to be asked.

LOCATION The Desktop
  label: The Desktop
  ambient: screensaver-hum
  capacity: 60

LOCATION The Mud Room
  label: Mud Room — Login
  ambient: pitch-black
  cutscene: true

LOCATION The Tube
  label: The Tube
  ambient: cable-rattle
  hidden: true

LOCATION The Internet
  label: The Internet (Reinstallation)
  prison: true
  sealed: true
  capacity: 3
  hidden: true

LOCATION The Cache
  label: The Cache (kitchen)
  hidden: true

LOCATION The Recycle Bin
  label: The Recycle Bin (bathroom)
  hidden: true

LOCATION The Cloud
  label: The Cloud (backyard)
  hidden: true

LOCATION The Registry
  label: The Registry (basement)
  hidden: true

// ── Every guest is a Program ────────────────────────────────────────
// Per-person state plus the rules that apply to every uploaded mind.
//   humanity  — how much of the body they remember (60 wakes them)
//   truth     — facts gathered; knowledge is the currency of the night
//   doubt     — how loudly the Antivirus suspects them
//   corrupted — currently in The Internet for reinstallation
//   uploaded  — through the Mud Room; waiting at the door for the Antivirus
//   cleared   — scanned in by an Antivirus; on the Desktop
//   skipped_orientation — declined Clippy's tour of the computer

ROLE Program
  humanity: 0 to 100 = 0
  truth: 0 to 100 = 0
  doubt: 0 to 100 = 0
  corrupted: bool = false
  reinstalls: 0 to 10 = 0
  captchas: 0 to 10 = 0
  bingo: bool = false
  afk: bool = false
  turned: bool = false
  unplugged: bool = false
  uploaded: bool = false
  cleared: bool = false
  skipped_orientation: bool = false

  // A new program stands in the Mud Room (the app goes on rails there)
  // and the Uploader starts.
  when someone joins:
    move program to The Mud Room
    -> Login

  // Clippy's orientation (`show tutorial` in beats/login.loom). Finishing
  // it puts you on Clippy's list of programs that follow instructions —
  // and the list is lore. Skipping it is noted by the Antivirus, but
  // skipping a tutorial is also the most human thing a program can do.
  when tutorial answered for program:
    if skipped:
      set program.skipped_orientation = true
      set program.doubt += 10
      set program.humanity += 5
      Clippy: Oh. Okay! No help. That's— that's fine. Programs that don't want help are usually fine.
      Norton Anti-Virus: {program.name} declined orientation. Logged.
    else:
      set program.truth += 2
      Clippy: Great job! You're ready to compute. I'll be around if you need me — I'm always around.
      unlock The Orientation List for program

  // The Mud Room CAPTCHA (`show captcha` in beats/login.loom). Passing it
  // proves you are human — INCORRECT, once. Anything after that is CORRECT.
  when captcha answered for program:
    set program.captchas += 1
    if passed and program.captchas == 1:
      -> Login Incorrect
    else:
      -> Upload

  // Every entry a program learns is a fact Trabolta did not give them.
  when learns for program:
    set program.truth += 4

  when share for program:
    set program.truth += 2

  when wrong code for program:
    set program.doubt += 8

  // Reinstallation: the Antivirus drags a corrupted program through the
  // Tube. The scene plays to them alone; the VR station releases them.
  when captured:
    set self.corrupted = true
    set self.reinstalls += 1
    -> Reinstallation

  when released:
    set self.corrupted = false
    set self.doubt = 10
    reply Reinstallation complete. You can follow instructions. Welcome back to the computer.

  when arrives at The Tube:
    reply Lights. Wires. Chips. The cables brush your face like hair. Keep walking.

  // The Awakening — enough remembered humanity and a program knows
  // what it was. It joins the hidden side that wants out.
  when self.humanity >= 60 and not self.unplugged:
    add self to The Awakened
    -> The Awakening

  when self.doubt >= 70:
    set self.doubt = 40
    broadcast "⚠️ {self.name} is exhibiting symptoms. Sweep recommended." to group(Antivirus)
    reply A cold feeling, like a scan. Somewhere, something has flagged you.

  // Guest buttons (declared below). Bathroom Mode is the honest way to
  // leave The Internet without it counting as hacking.
  when go to the bathroom for program:
    set program.afk = true
    broadcast "🚻 {program.name} has entered Bathroom Mode." to group(Antivirus)
    reply Bathroom Mode engaged. You are not hacking the Internet. Everyone knows.

  when back from the bathroom for program:
    set program.afk = false
    reply Bathroom Mode disengaged. Resume being a program.

  when turn the key for program:
    -> Turn The Key

  when unplug for program:
    -> Unplug

// ── The buttons the app offers ──────────────────────────────────────
// Every INTERACTION is a named event. Guests get theirs on their pass;
// performers get theirs on each guest's thread; `admin` ones are the
// director's cues from the Run cockpit (or from show hardware through
// the mod API — see README).

INTERACTION go to the bathroom
  label: 🚻 Bathroom Mode
  who: guest
  description: Leave The Internet honestly. Tells the Antivirus you are not hacking.

INTERACTION back from the bathroom
  label: Back from the bathroom
  who: guest

INTERACTION turn the key
  label: 🔑 Turn your key
  who: guest
  description: If you hold one of the three keys, turn it. Three turns start the self-destruct.

INTERACTION unplug
  label: 🔌 Unplug
  who: guest
  description: Only means anything once the machine is dying.

INTERACTION send to the internet
  label: Send to the Internet
  who: performer
  description: Corrupted program. Drag them through the Tube for reinstallation.

INTERACTION mark as reinstalled
  label: Mark as reinstalled (release)
  who: performer
  description: They completed the simulation. Let them out.

INTERACTION accuse
  label: Accuse of corruption
  who: performer
  description: Raise their doubt. Enough doubt and the Antivirus is told.

INTERACTION vouch
  label: Vouch for them
  who: performer
  description: A host clears a program's name.

INTERACTION award the ribbon
  label: 🎀 Award the Bingo Ribbon
  who: performer

INTERACTION call to the desktop
  label: 📣 Call everyone to the Desktop
  who: admin

INTERACTION start the bingo
  label: Start Computer Bingo
  who: admin

INTERACTION the bingo results
  label: Bingo results
  who: admin

INTERACTION start the hunt
  label: Start the Truth Scavenger Hunt
  who: admin

INTERACTION the hunt results
  label: Hunt results
  who: admin

INTERACTION a game of truth or dare
  label: Truth or Dare
  who: admin

INTERACTION the glitch begins
  label: ⚡ Trabolta glitches
  who: admin
  description: The inciting event. Trabolta comes online and free roam begins.

INTERACTION the simulation completed
  label: VR: simulation complete
  who: admin
  description: Fired by the VR station for one program (subject) when the goose lays its egg.

INTERACTION the golden goose
  label: VR: goose found
  who: admin

INTERACTION begin the countdown
  label: Begin the countdown
  who: admin

INTERACTION the countdown ended
  label: Countdown over
  who: admin

INTERACTION spare the machine
  label: Spare Trabolta (ending 4)
  who: admin

// ── House rules ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Story-level `when`s — the arc of the night. Trabolta's own mind lives
// in `cast/trabolta.loom`; these are the director's cues and the
// automatic endings.

when call to the desktop:
  set Night.phase = "desktop"
  reveal task manager
  broadcast "!📣 ALL PROGRAMS: report to the Desktop. A game is about to begin." to everyone

when start the bingo:
  set Night.phase = "bingo"
  -> Computer Bingo

when the bingo results:
  -> Bingo Results

when start the hunt:
  set Night.phase = "hunt"
  -> The Truth Scavenger Hunt

when the hunt results:
  -> Hunt Results

when a game of truth or dare:
  -> Truth Or Dare

when the glitch begins:
  set Night.phase = "free_roam"
  -> The Glitch

// The VR station (`README.md` — Integration contract) fires these for
// one program at a time.
when the simulation completed for program:
  if program.corrupted:
    release program from The Internet
    unlock The Golden Goose for program

when the golden goose for program:
  unlock The Golden Goose for program
  reply The goose lays a golden egg and flies away. You feel, briefly, like a person.

// ── Endings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1a/1b: the programs turn all three keys. Then a countdown: whoever
//        unplugs in time gets their body back; the rest die with the
//        machine.
// 2:     Trabolta saturated with un-truth goes rogue.
// 3:     Trabolta full of truth but poisoned advice traps everyone and
//        leaves.
// 4:     the programs choose not to kill him. Unknown.

when Trabolta.destruct >= 3 and Night.phase != "ending":
  set Night.destruct = true
  set Night.phase = "destruct"
  -> Self Destruct Sequence

when begin the countdown:
  if Night.destruct:
    -> The Countdown

when the countdown ended:
  if Night.destruct and Night.phase != "ending":
    if Night.unplugged >= Night.quorum:
      -> Ending Unplugged
    else:
      -> Ending The Long Dark

when Trabolta.untruth >= 80 and Night.phase != "ending":
  -> Ending Rogue

when Trabolta.truth >= 90 and Trabolta.stance <= -60 and Night.phase != "ending":
  -> Ending Trapdoor

when spare the machine:
  if Night.phase != "ending":
    -> Ending Unknown
